# atomic sandbox replay v1
# M5 "Drag far -> fallback lights up, the model learns" and fix rounds 3-4 "once it falls back it
# comes back" (re-check by hand: drag H2 far apart while playing, then let go): the estimated
# solver samples H2 (the automatic pass, about 40 s) and plays on the model; with nucleus 1 pinned
# (so the pull stretches the bond instead of towing the molecule) a Select-drag pulls nucleus 0
# out toward 3.34 Bohr from nucleus 1 and holds it there for 20 fs, then brings the cursor back to
# where nucleus 0 started and holds 20 fs more before letting go; the wheel during the drag
# raises the pull from 0.1 to 0.1 x 1.25^5 = 0.305 Ha/Bohr (UI checklist "drag pull").
# Asserted: the pull; the bond stretched past 2.8 Bohr; at least one step since the mark was a
# DFT fallback; after the release the model answers again (`wait source surrogate`, polled), it
# kept at least one new sample and refitted at least once, and after 400 more steps at most 10 %
# of the last 100 steps fell back (a ratio: the single latest step flickers while playing).
# Paced by the simulation, never the wall clock (M6 pre-merge fix). The drag used to be held for
# `wait ms` (5 x 50 ms ramp, 1500 ms hold); once the stretch leaves the model's trust every step
# is a DFT fallback (79 ms on a free GPU, 317 ms on a shared one), so the stretch reached and the
# energy the pull injects followed the GPU load: a busy GPU stretched only to 2.55 Bohr, another
# run reached 3.18 Bohr and left the molecule hot enough (E 0.074 Ha above the start) to reach
# the cell's margin with the walls off, which paused the run at step 328. Now each ramp move
# waits 2 steps (0.5 fs at dt = 0.25 fs) and the hold is `wait fs 20` (80 steps): the drag's
# schedule is fixed in simulated time (model answers are deterministic, fallbacks synchronous);
# only the step an input lands on can move by one (a step in flight finishes before the worker
# reads the next command). The walls are on at 4.5 Bohr (the app's default for this 49^3 x 0.25
# cell; a sim-side potential that never reaches the teacher's labels; its soft layer starts at
# 3.5 Bohr, beyond the drag target at x = 2.54 Bohr), so whatever the pull leaves in the molecule
# bounces off them instead of reaching the cell's 3h margin. The 2.8 Bohr bound is the one this
# script was written with, not re-derived: on this schedule the stretch crosses it about 5 fs into
# the hold and the critically damped pull settles at rest near 3.44 Bohr (measured; the replayer
# logs max-dist, so the margin stays visible). Why the cursor comes back before the release: let
# go at 3.44 Bohr from rest, the NVE pair (E 0.082 Ha above the start) returns to 3.44 Bohr every
# vibration (about 58 steps), and the model falls back near that turning point each time (the
# envelope's thinned samples do not extend its trust there; measured: the last 100 steps held one
# or two such windows, 6-12 % through the run), so `fallback-fraction 0.1` passed or failed with
# the vibration's phase at the check. Brought back by the damped spring, the pair is released
# near rest inside the trained range, and the check measures recovery, not phase.
view 1400 900
action smooth-motion false
# pinned at the merge of main (2026-10-14): written for the presets' own 49^3 x 0.25 grid (Balanced),
# before the app defaulted to Accurate (81^3); the walls are pinned on (above); H2 is the
# R = 1.6 Bohr scene it was written for (h2_r16.scene; the h2 preset is 1.45 Bohr now)
action quality balanced
action walls on 4.5
scene h2_r16.scene
wait idle
action backend estimated
wait idle
action tool select
t 100 cursor 0.1043005 0.0244677
action play
wait steps 20
mark
action pin 1 true
t 200 button left down
t 210 wheel 5
t 240 cursor 0.1543005 0.0244677
wait steps 2
t 290 cursor 0.2043005 0.0244677
wait steps 2
t 340 cursor 0.2543005 0.0244677
wait steps 2
t 390 cursor 0.3043005 0.0244677
wait steps 2
t 440 cursor 0.3543005 0.0244677
wait steps 2
t 490 cursor 0.4043005 0.0244677
wait fs 20
expect pull 0.30 0.31
expect max-dist 0 1 2.8
expect fallbacks 1
t 1990 cursor 0.1043005 0.0244677
wait fs 20
t 2010 button left up
action pin 1 false
wait source surrogate
wait steps 400
expect new-samples 1
expect new-epochs 1
expect fallback-fraction 0.1
action pause
wait idle
expect no-error
# Activity tab (activity spec §8): the fallbacks of the drag reached the solve log and the counters
expect solve-log 1
expect counters
